<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 154 0 R
/E (Business user authentication proceeds through phone OTP verification. The user selects role and enters their phone number with country code. Firebase Authentication's verifyPhoneNumber dispatches the SMS OTP. The user enters the 6-digit code in a Pinput widget with a 60-second countdown resend timer. Upon verification, a Firestore user document is created with isProfileComplete set to false, triggering navigation to the role- appropriate profile setup screen.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 154 0 R
/E (Customer authentication proceeds as follows: the user selects Customer role and is directed to the Google Auth screen. The GoogleSignIn SDK initiates the OAuth 2.0 flow. Access and ID tokens are retrieved and a Firebase AuthCredential is constructed. Firebase Authentication verifies the credential and creates the session. The application checks Firestore for existing profile; new users receive an auto-created profile with isProfileComplete set to true and are navigated to the main application.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 154 0 R
/E (Token Management: Firebase Authentication manages JWT token generation, refresh, and expiration automatically. Profile Completion Guard: PopScope-based navigation guard prevents access to the main application without completing business profile registration. Input Validation: All user inputs are validated at the Flutter form level using TextFormField validators before Firestore submission, including required field checks, minimum length constraints, and format validation.)
/Pg 27 0 R
